## Context and authority

Filed from replicator (closed ticket 0008, main eded457) at the author's
request on 2026-11-26. Integration-review finding for tracker 1552. The
author ruled the review style suitable and asked for a committed verdict
("C'est bien identifié ou pas ?"). Request for receiving Imagine only.

## Observation

The I4R six-row table rates computation only; identification critiques
live in the report's prose, and the skill has no verb or section for
them. Replicator 0008 added, for Carter (2024) Figure 5:

- a causal DAG (`identification/dag.svg`) with conventions in
  `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator/doc/identification-method.md`;
- an 11-item checklist of Pearl-style confounder-handling errors
  (bad controls, colliders, post-treatment conditioning, compound
  treatment, misclassification, sensitivity bounds), each with two
  plain-language sentences for non-specialist economists;
- a committed verdict on a four-step scale (well / plausibly / weakly /
  not identified) plus a labelled subjective probability (here:
  plausibly identified, not established; 60% / 65%).

A cross-family review seat caught two reasoning errors both favourable to
the authors ("smooth, therefore absorbed" fails against a province-level
jump at a geographic border; pre-treatment road evidence wrongly called
post-treatment). Lesson: this review needs a decorrelated seat.

Evidence: `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator/replications/carter2024-mainclaim-cra/identification/`
(checklist.md, dag.svg, index.html), `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator/doc/identification-method.md`.

## Proposed (for Imagine to accept, amend or reject)

An identification section, under `report` (or a step of `probe`), kept
out of the ACRe score and the six-row table: DAG, checklist, verdict
scale, plain-language explanations, cross-family review seat. The method
document could move to `skills/replicate/references/`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Receiving Imagine records facts, duplicates, ownership, rulings
  (rule 4 fairness: a robust verdict is as valuable as a fragile one).
- [ ] If accepted: the section is placed, the scale and checklist are
  referenced, and the score/table remain computation-only.
- [ ] Verdict wording never presented as a reproducibility status.
